-- Migration 0028 (rescue-4 round-3): replace the legal-template bodies with
-- COMPREHENSIVE, legally-protective copy (v2 over 0025).
--
-- The public renderer renderPageHtml (api/src/public/render-pages.ts) outputs a
-- legal page body RAW and PREFERS legal_templates.content_html. It also
-- SUPPRESSES the wrapper page title when the body already opens with its own
-- leading <h1> (render-pages.ts: bodyLeadsWithH1 = /^\s*<h1[\s>]/i), so each
-- content_html below STARTS with <h1>Title</h1> to render exactly one heading.
--
-- HARD TOKEN CONSTRAINT: substituteLegalTemplate substitutes ONLY these 6
-- tokens and STRIPS every other {{...}} (RESIDUAL_PLACEHOLDER_RE):
--   {{site_name}} {{domain}} {{contact_email}} {{privacy_email}}
--   {{effective_date}} {{company_name}}
-- So this copy uses ONLY those 6, and contains NO other {{...}} and NO
-- "[bracket]" placeholders, NO physical mailing address, NO named
-- governing-law state or court, NO founding year, NO phone number (these sites
-- are email-only and jurisdiction-neutral). The Do-Not-Sell opt-out BUTTON is
-- injected at render time by the app, not stored here.
--
-- Prose is APOSTROPHE-FREE (formal legal register: "we" / "do not" / "the
-- rights of users" instead of contractions and possessive apostrophes) so the
-- single-quoted SQL string literals need no escaping. Idempotent UPDATE by
-- unique slug.

UPDATE legal_templates SET content_html = '<h1>Privacy Policy</h1><p><em>Last updated: {{effective_date}}</em></p><p>This Privacy Policy explains how {{company_name}} collects, uses, discloses, and protects information when you access {{site_name}} at {{domain}} and any related websites and services. By using the services you agree to the practices described here. In this policy the words "we", "us", and "our" refer to {{company_name}}.</p><h2>Information we collect</h2><h3>Information you provide</h3><p>We collect information you choose to give us, such as your email address when you subscribe to a newsletter, the content of messages you send us, and any details you include in a request or survey response.</p><h3>Information collected automatically</h3><p>When you visit {{domain}} we automatically collect technical and usage data such as your IP address, browser type and version, operating system, device type, referring and exit pages, the pages you view, and the approximate region derived from your IP address. This data is collected through server logs and similar technologies and is used in aggregate.</p><h3>Cookies and similar technologies</h3><p>We use cookies, pixels, and web beacons to operate the site, remember your preferences, measure traffic, and support advertising. Session cookies expire when you close your browser, while persistent cookies remain until they expire or you delete them. Advertising partners may place their own cookies. You can disable cookies in your browser settings, although some features may not work as intended.</p><h3>Information from third parties</h3><p>We may receive information about you from advertising networks, analytics providers, and other publicly available sources, and we may combine it with information we already hold.</p><h2>How we use information</h2><p>We use the information we collect to operate, maintain, and improve {{site_name}}, to send the newsletters and replies you request, to understand which content is useful, to measure and improve performance, to deliver and measure advertising, to detect and prevent fraud and abuse, to enforce our terms, and to comply with legal obligations. We do not sell your personal information for money. See the Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information page for the choices available to you.</p><h2>How we disclose information</h2><h3>Service providers</h3><p>We share information with vendors that perform services on our behalf, such as hosting, content delivery, analytics, and email delivery. These providers are permitted to use the information only to provide the agreed services.</p><h3>Advertising networks</h3><p>Some pages display advertising from third-party networks. These partners may use cookies and similar technologies to deliver relevant ads and to measure their performance under their own privacy policies.</p><h3>Legal and safety</h3><p>We may disclose information when required by law, regulation, legal process, or governmental request, or when we believe in good faith that disclosure is necessary to enforce our terms, to protect the rights, property, or safety of users or the public, or to prevent fraud or illegal activity.</p><h3>Business transfers</h3><p>If we are involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, reorganization, or sale of assets, information may be transferred as part of that transaction, subject to this policy.</p><h2>Third-party links</h2><p>Our services may contain links to websites and services that we do not operate. We are not responsible for the privacy practices or the content of those third parties. We encourage you to review the privacy policy of every site you visit. Your use of third-party sites is at your own risk.</p><h2>Data retention</h2><p>We retain personal information only for as long as needed to provide the services, to fulfil the purposes described in this policy, to resolve disputes, and to comply with our legal obligations. When information is no longer needed we delete it or anonymize it, unless retention is required by law.</p><h2>Data security</h2><p>We use reasonable physical, technical, and administrative measures designed to protect personal information, including encryption in transit and access controls. However, no system is impenetrable, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. You provide information to us at your own risk. If a breach occurs that affects you, we will notify you as required by applicable law.</p><h2>Your rights and choices</h2><p>Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access the personal information we hold about you, to receive a copy in a portable format, to correct inaccurate information, to request deletion, and to opt out of the sale or sharing of your information. You can opt out of marketing emails using the unsubscribe link in any such email. To make a privacy request, email {{privacy_email}}, and we will respond within the time the law requires.</p><h2>European Economic Area and United Kingdom rights (GDPR)</h2><p>If you are located in the European Economic Area or the United Kingdom, we process your personal information under the General Data Protection Regulation and equivalent United Kingdom law. Our legal bases include your consent, the performance of a service you request, our legitimate interests in operating and improving the services, and compliance with legal obligations. You have the right to access, correct, delete, restrict, or object to processing, to data portability, to withdraw consent at any time, and to lodge a complaint with your local supervisory authority. Where we transfer information internationally we rely on appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses. To exercise these rights, email {{privacy_email}}.</p><h2>United States state privacy rights</h2><p>If you are a resident of California, you have rights under the California Consumer Privacy Act as amended by the California Privacy Rights Act, including the right to know what personal information we collect and how we use and disclose it, the right to delete it, the right to correct it, the right to opt out of its sale or sharing, the right to limit the use of sensitive personal information, and the right not to be discriminated against for exercising these rights. Residents of other states with comprehensive privacy laws may have similar rights to access, delete, correct, port, and opt out of targeted advertising and the sale of personal information. To exercise any of these rights, email {{privacy_email}}, and we will verify and respond to your request as the law requires. You may use an authorized agent where the law permits.</p><h2>Childrens privacy</h2><p>Our services are not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If we learn that we have collected such information without verifiable parental consent, we will delete it promptly. A parent or guardian who believes a child under 13 has provided us information may contact {{privacy_email}}.</p><h2>International users</h2><p>We operate the services from the United States, and information we collect may be transferred to, stored in, and processed in the United States or other countries whose data-protection laws may differ from those of your country. By using the services you understand that your information may be processed in those locations.</p><h2>Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes are posted on this page with a revised last-updated date. Your continued use of the services after a change takes effect means that you accept the updated policy.</p><h2>Contact us</h2><p>For questions about this policy or our data practices, email {{privacy_email}}.</p>' WHERE slug = 'privacy-policy';

UPDATE legal_templates SET content_html = '<h1>Terms of Use</h1><p><em>Last updated: {{effective_date}}</em></p><p>These Terms of Use ("Terms") form a binding agreement between you and {{company_name}} and govern your access to and use of {{site_name}} at {{domain}} and any related websites, content, features, and services (the "services"). By accessing or using the services you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the services. In these Terms the words "we", "us", and "our" refer to {{company_name}}.</p><h2>Eligibility</h2><p>You represent that you are at least 13 years old, or the age of majority where you live, and that you are able to form a binding contract. If you are under 18 you confirm that you have the consent of a parent or guardian or that you use the services under their supervision.</p><h2>Permitted use</h2><p>We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to access and view the services for your personal, non-commercial use, subject to these Terms.</p><h2>Prohibited conduct</h2><p>You agree not to use the services to do any of the following:</p><ul><li>Post or transmit material that is unlawful, defamatory, obscene, threatening, harassing, hateful, or that infringes the rights of others.</li><li>Send spam, unsolicited advertising, or harmful code such as viruses or malware.</li><li>Use bots, scrapers, spiders, or other automated means to access or extract data from the services.</li><li>Reverse engineer, decompile, or attempt to discover the source code or underlying technology of the services.</li><li>Bypass or interfere with access controls, authentication, or the normal operation of our servers and networks.</li><li>Attempt to gain unauthorized access to any account, system, or data.</li><li>Impersonate any person or misrepresent your identity, or collect information about others without consent.</li><li>Violate any applicable law or regulation.</li></ul><p>We may investigate suspected violations and may remove content, suspend or terminate access, or disclose information to authorities as we reasonably believe necessary to enforce these Terms or to comply with the law. We are not obligated to monitor user conduct and do not guarantee the removal of all prohibited material.</p><h2>Intellectual property</h2><p>All content on {{site_name}}, including text, images, audio, video, graphics, logos, layout, and code, is owned by {{company_name}} or its licensors and is protected by intellectual-property laws. Except as expressly permitted, you may not reproduce, modify, distribute, publicly display, create derivative works from, or commercially exploit any content without our prior written permission, and you may not remove any proprietary notices.</p><h2>User content</h2><p>If you submit, post, or upload content to the services, you grant {{company_name}} a worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free, perpetual, and irrevocable license to use, reproduce, modify, adapt, publish, translate, create derivative works from, distribute, and display that content in any media. You represent and warrant that you own or have all rights necessary to grant this license and that your content does not infringe the rights of any third party or violate any law. This license survives the termination of your access.</p><h2>Advertising and affiliate disclosure</h2><p>The services may display advertising and may contain affiliate links for which {{company_name}} receives compensation. We may earn a commission when you purchase through an affiliate link, which does not change the price you pay. We make these disclosures in accordance with applicable advertising rules.</p><h2>No professional advice</h2><p>The content on the services is provided for general information and entertainment only and does not constitute professional advice, whether legal, medical, financial, tax, or otherwise. Do not rely on the content as a substitute for advice from a qualified professional. Always consult a qualified professional about your particular situation. {{company_name}} is not responsible for actions taken on the basis of the content.</p><h2>Disclaimer of warranties</h2><p>THE SERVICES AND ALL CONTENT ARE PROVIDED ON AN "AS IS" AND "AS AVAILABLE" BASIS WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED. TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, {{company_name}} DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES, INCLUDING THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT. WE DO NOT WARRANT THAT THE SERVICES WILL BE UNINTERRUPTED, TIMELY, SECURE, OR ERROR-FREE, OR THAT THE CONTENT IS ACCURATE, COMPLETE, OR CURRENT.</p><h2>Limitation of liability</h2><p>TO THE FULLEST EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, IN NO EVENT WILL {{company_name}} OR ITS OFFICERS, DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AGENTS, OR AFFILIATES BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, OR FOR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, GOODWILL, OR BUSINESS, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICES, EVEN IF WE HAVE BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. SOME JURISDICTIONS DO NOT ALLOW THE EXCLUSION OR LIMITATION OF CERTAIN DAMAGES, SO SOME OF THE ABOVE MAY NOT APPLY TO YOU.</p><h2>Indemnification</h2><p>You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless {{company_name}} and its officers, directors, employees, agents, licensors, and affiliates from any claims, damages, liabilities, costs, and expenses, including reasonable legal fees, arising out of or related to your use of the services, your content, your violation of these Terms or any law, or your infringement of the rights of any third party. This obligation survives the termination of your access.</p><h2>Copyright complaints</h2><p>We respond to notices of alleged copyright infringement in accordance with the Digital Millennium Copyright Act and other applicable law. If you believe that content on the services infringes your copyright, send a notice to {{contact_email}} that includes a description of the work, the location of the material on the services, your contact information, a statement of your good-faith belief that the use is not authorized, a statement under penalty of perjury that your notice is accurate and that you are authorized to act, and your physical or electronic signature.</p><h2>Termination</h2><p>We may suspend or terminate your access to the services at any time, with or without notice, if we reasonably believe you have violated these Terms or applicable law or to protect the services, our users, or our business. Upon termination your right to use the services ends immediately. Provisions that by their nature should survive, including intellectual property, disclaimers, limitation of liability, and indemnification, will survive.</p><h2>Dispute resolution and class-action waiver</h2><p>Before bringing any formal claim, you agree to first contact us and attempt in good faith to resolve the dispute informally. To the fullest extent permitted by law, you and {{company_name}} agree that any dispute will be resolved on an individual basis only, and each of you waives any right to participate in a class action, class-wide arbitration, or any other representative proceeding. Claims must be brought in an individual capacity.</p><h2>Severability</h2><p>If any provision of these Terms is held to be invalid or unenforceable, that provision will be limited or removed to the minimum extent necessary, and the remaining provisions will continue in full force and effect.</p><h2>Changes to these Terms</h2><p>We may update these Terms from time to time. Changes take effect when posted on this page with a revised last-updated date. Your continued use of the services after a change takes effect means that you accept the updated Terms.</p><h2>Contact us</h2><p>For questions about these Terms, or to report a violation or abuse, email {{contact_email}}.</p>' WHERE slug = 'terms';

UPDATE legal_templates SET content_html = '<h1>Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information</h1><p>{{company_name}} does not sell your personal information for money. However, some online advertising can count as a sale or as sharing under laws such as the California Consumer Privacy Act and the California Privacy Rights Act, because advertising partners may use cookies and similar technologies to build a profile and deliver personalized ads across different websites. This page explains those practices and how you can opt out.</p><h2>What we sell or share</h2><p>When you use {{site_name}} we may allow advertising and analytics partners to receive identifiers such as cookie and device identifiers, your IP address, the pages you view and the content you engage with, and inferences about your interests, so that they can deliver and measure cross-context behavioral advertising. We do not share sensitive personal information for these advertising purposes.</p><h2>How to opt out</h2><p>You can opt out of the sale or sharing of your personal information for advertising on this site. An opt-out control is provided on this page by the application. When you use it, we signal our advertising partners not to sell or share your information and we store your choice in a cookie on this device. Because the choice is stored in a cookie, it applies only to this browser and device, so if you clear your cookies or use another device you will need to set it again. You can also email {{privacy_email}} to submit an opt-out request or to ask about the personal information we hold about you.</p><h2>Industry opt-out tools</h2><p>You can also limit interest-based advertising across many companies using industry tools such as the opt-out pages operated by the Network Advertising Initiative and the Digital Advertising Alliance, and by adjusting the advertising and privacy settings on your device and browser.</p><h2>Global Privacy Control</h2><p>We honor the Global Privacy Control. If your browser or a browser extension sends a Global Privacy Control signal, we treat it as a valid request to opt out of the sale and sharing of personal information for that browser.</p><h2>Non-discrimination</h2><p>We will not discriminate against you for exercising your privacy rights. You will receive the same content, services, and quality whether or not you opt out.</p><h2>Other rights and contact</h2><p>You may also have the right to access, correct, or delete the personal information we hold about you. To exercise any of these rights, or for questions about this page, email {{privacy_email}}.</p>' WHERE slug = 'do-not-sell';

UPDATE legal_templates SET content_html = '<h1>Contact Us</h1><p>We would love to hear from you. {{site_name}} is operated by {{company_name}}, and the fastest way to reach us is by email. The sections below explain which address to use so that your message reaches the right place. We do not offer support by post or telephone.</p><h2>General inquiries and support</h2><p>For questions, feedback, suggestions, or general support, email {{contact_email}}. Please include a clear subject and a short description of your question so that we can help you quickly. We read every message and aim to reply within a few business days.</p><h2>Privacy requests</h2><p>For privacy questions and to exercise your data rights, including requests to access, correct, delete, or stop the sale or sharing of your personal information, email {{privacy_email}}. Tell us the nature of your request so that we can verify and process it as the law requires.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>If you spot something inaccurate in our content, email {{contact_email}} with the title of the article and the detail you believe is wrong. We correct genuine mistakes promptly.</p><h2>Copyright and DMCA notices</h2><p>To report content that you believe infringes your copyright, email {{contact_email}} with the subject "Copyright Notice". Include a description of the work, the location of the material on {{site_name}}, your contact information, a statement of your good-faith belief that the use is not authorized, a statement under penalty of perjury that your notice is accurate and that you are authorized to act, and your signature.</p><h2>Abuse and policy violations</h2><p>To report spam, harassment, abusive content, or other violations of our terms, email {{contact_email}} with the subject "Abuse Report" and include the relevant links and a description of the problem.</p><h2>Advertising and partnerships</h2><p>For advertising, sponsorship, or partnership inquiries, email {{contact_email}} with a short summary of your proposal. We review every serious inquiry and respond when there is a good fit.</p>' WHERE slug = 'contact';
